\ complex — a pair of floats, real and imaginary. Literals 3+4i / 4i;
\ + - * / over complexes and floats (floats promote losslessly); negate
\ keeps the type, abs answers the modulus; ordering is by real part then
\ imaginary part, and a complex equals a float of its value.

\ === literals, printing, destructuring ===

3+4i . -1.5-2i . 4i . 2e3+0.5i . cr           \ 3+4i -1.5-2i 0+4i 2000+0.5i
3+4i type-of . 3+4i complex? . 5 complex? . cr  \ :complex 1 0
1 2 complex . cr                              \ 1+2i
3+4i real-part . 3+4i imaginary-part . cr     \ 3 4
5 real-part . 5 imaginary-part . cr           \ 5 0

clear
\ === arithmetic; floats promote ===

1+2i 3+4i + . 1+2i 3+4i - . cr                \ 4+6i -2-2i
1+2i 3+4i * . 1+1i 1-1i * . cr                \ -5+10i 2+0i
10+5i 2 / . 2 1i * . cr                       \ 5+2.5i 0+2i
1+2i 3 + . 3 1+2i - . cr                      \ 4+2i 2-2i
3+4i abs . 3+4i negate . cr                   \ 5 -3-4i
1+2i 1+ . 1+2i 1- . 1+2i sq . cr              \ 2+2i 0+2i -3+4i
0+0i not . 1i not . 3+4i nan? . cr            \ 1 0 0

clear
\ === transcendentals answer principal values ===

-1+0i sqrt . 0+2i sqrt . cr                   \ 0+1i 1+1i
-1+0i ln . 100+0i log . 0+0i exp . cr         \ 0+3.14159i 2+0i 1+0i
1i sin . 1i cos . cr                          \ 0+1.1752i 1.54308+0i
2+0i asin . cr                                \ 1.5708+1.31696i (leaves the real interval)
1i 2 ^ . 1+1i 1+1i ^ . cr                     \ -1+1.22465e-16i 0.273957+0.583701i

clear
\ === comparison and collections ===

3+4i 3+4i = . 3+4i 3+5i = . 3+0i 3 = . cr     \ 1 0 1
2+1i 2+2i < . 2+2i 2+1i < . cr                \ 1 0 (structural order: real part, then imaginary)
[ 2+1i 1+5i 1+2i 0.5 ] sort . cr              \ [ 0.5 1+2i 1+5i 2+1i ]
[< 1+2i 1+2i 2+3i >] . cr                     \ [< 1+2i 2+3i >]
{ :z 1+2i } :z @ . cr                         \ 1+2i
1+2i "{0} volts" format . cr                  \ 1+2i volts
[ 1+2i 3+4i ] [: 1i * :] map . cr             \ [ -2+1i -4+3i ]
[ 1+1i 2+2i ] 0+0i ' + reduce . cr            \ 3+3i
[ 1+2i 3+4i 5+6i 7+8i ] [: 2 * :] pmap . cr   \ [ 2+4i 6+8i 10+12i 14+16i ]
: twiddle 1+2i ; gc twiddle . cr              \ 1+2i (a compiled literal survives collection)

clear
\ === complex magnitudes take units (impedance) ===

base unit ohm
3+4i ohm . 3+4i ohm abs . 3+4i ohm negate . cr  \ 3+4i ohm 5 ohm -3-4i ohm
3+4i ohm 1+1i ohm + . 3+4i ohm 1 ohm - . cr   \ 4+5i ohm 2+4i ohm
3+4i ohm 2+0i ohm / . 1+1i ohm 2 * . cr       \ 1.5+2i 2+2i ohm
1+1i km 500 m + . 1000+1000i m 1+1i km = . cr \ 1.5+1i km 1
0+4i m 0+4i m * . 1+1i hour 2 m * . cr        \ -16+0i m^2 7200+7200i m.s

clear
\ === errors (each reason parenthesized) ===

1+2i 0 /                                      \ (division by zero)
1+2i 1/2 +                                    \ (exacts and complexes stay apart)
1+2i vector                                   \ (matrices stay float)
1+2i lgamma                                   \ (lgamma takes floats and matrices only)
1+2i round                                    \ (the rounding words reject complexes)
1+2i m 1/2 m +                                \ (exact and complex magnitudes stay apart)
